istinguish an exhausted pool from an unobserved one","claim":"The function treats any `AcquireOutcome::Refused` as \"capacity never observed\" and, under `SerializeConservatively`, calls `define_pool(..., 1, false)` for every unavailable request — including pools that are already defined and merely contended, and including byte-denominated pools such as `AcceleratorMemory` where a capacity of 1 is meaningless.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs","range":{"start":108,"end":131}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs","range":{"start":67,"end":106}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:84c242bcf89e5a088cc440c45bcf0591b6cc825687758df7445d784a96e20210","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":110888,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-63","revision":"sha256:8b8dbc823cd8b7b46d8e70ee0e132e832a59585324193736c5669d00b834d380","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-84c242bcf89e5a088cc440c45bcf0591b6cc825687758df7445d784a96e20210-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Query pool existence explicitly (or have the repository distinguish `PoolUndefined` from `Insufficient`) before applying the unknown-capacity policy, and bootstrap only slot-denominated resources; a worker whose 8192 MB accelerator pool is temporarily full must not be routed through the unknown-capacity branch. The disclosed tests never cover a defined-but-exhausted pool reaching this branch, so the behaviour when `define_pool` is re-called on an existing pool is unverified here.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F4-tls-field-unenforced","category":"security_issue","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"`LocalEndpointConfig.tls` is never read and no scheme check guards bearer credentials on non