df7445d784a96e20210","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":110888,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-63","revision":"sha256:8b8dbc823cd8b7b46d8e70ee0e132e832a59585324193736c5669d00b834d380","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-84c242bcf89e5a088cc440c45bcf0591b6cc825687758df7445d784a96e20210-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Use a `BTreeMap<u64, _>` (or emit in first-seen index order) so completion events follow the backend's `index` ordering deterministically, and add a fake-runtime test with two parallel tool calls asserting the event order.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F6-new-crates-not-covered-by-passing-check","category":"unverifiable_claim","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"The two crates holding most of the new code are not covered by any passing verification check","claim":"The required `tests-green-crates` check runs only `familiar-ai-core`, `familiar-ai-review`, `familiar-ai-agent` and `familiar-ai-storage`; the ~1,600 new lines in `familiar-ai-llm/src/local_runtime.rs` and `familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs` plus `familiar-ai-daemon/tests/local_worker_runtime.rs` are exercised only by `tests-workspace-advisory`, which exited 101 (failed), so I cannot confirm the new daemon/LLM tests pass or that this change did not break existing workspace tests.","evidence":[{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:84c242bcf89e5a088cc440c45bcf0591b6cc825687758df7445d784a96e20210","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":110888,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-63","revision":"sha256:8b8dbc823cd8b7b46d8e70ee0e132e832a59585324193736c5669d00b834d380","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-84c242bcf89e5a088cc440c45bcf059