/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-714ca437af863f7ff5eedefd379ab4b94405e3ffe060865df77c7be94c3014ca-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/registry_workers.rs","range":{"start":246,"end":383}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs","range":{"start":67,"end":106}}],"remediation":"Either wire the registry's `local` profile into worker construction and pool definition (deriving `InferenceSlots`/`ModelLoadingSlots` capacity from `concurrent_inference_slots`/`model_loading_slots`) and show the production call site, or state plainly in the contract's scope section that phase 1 ships the adapter and scheduling primitives unwired, and drop or mark as unread the resource fields nothing consumes.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F8-memory-pressure-test-covers-no-local-code","category":"test_gap","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"The memory-pressure test exercises only PRD-064's own settle API, not any local-worker code","claim":"`mid_run_memory_pressure_is_recorded_as_honest_overrun` defines a pool, acquires directly through `ReservationRepository::acquire`, then calls `repo.settle` with a hand-written larger observation and asserts `settled.overrun`; no function from `local_worker_runtime` (and no memory-pressure detection, refusal, or capacity-revocation path in the local adapter) is under test, so the acceptance criteria for memory-pressure refusals, queue depth and concurrency limits, and capacity revocation have no coverage.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/local_worker_runtime.rs","range":{"start":250,"end":300}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs","range":{"start":183,"end":215}}],"remediation":"Add tests that drive a memory-pressure/queue-depth/revocation signal through the local code path (e.g. a fake endpoint returning a load-failure