## Remediation summary

**F1 (retries miscounted as attempts) — already fixed on entry, verified correct.** `persist_local_telemetry` now takes an explicit `retries: u32` parameter instead of deriving it from `outcome.attempts.len()`. Confirmed no other call site in the workspace still derives retries from attempt count.

**F4 (TLS field unenforced) — already fixed on entry, verified correct.** `LocalEndpointConfig::tls` is now validated against the URL's actual scheme (`base_url_uses_https`), non-loopback endpoints require both `tls = true` and an `https://` URL, and `LocalChatClient::new` refuses to attach a bearer credential to any non-loopback endpoint that isn't HTTPS.

**F6 (uncovered crates) — investigated and resolved as far as scope allows.** Ran `familiar-ai-llm` and `familiar-ai-daemon`'s full test suites (in Docker and locally): all pass except one pre-existing, unrelated flake — `daemon_starts_and_stops_on_sigterm` in `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/integration.rs`, a process-spawn test with a fixed wall-clock startup budget that misses under Docker CPU contention (same failure class as the already-documented FAM-BUG-047; it passes reliably on bare host). It touches no code from this diff. I can't edit the `tests-green-crates` command itself (it lives in verification-plan config outside `crates/`), so I can't add these crates to the required gate.

**F7 (unwired local worker) — partially resolved; one real gap remains that I did not paper over.** I confirmed via research that *no* raw-runtime adapter — Anthropic, OpenAI, xAI, or Local — has a production caller anywhere in this codebase; the daemon's actual execution path (`run.rs`) dispatches a completely separate subprocess-based `CodingAgent` system that has no bridge to `raw_runtime::run_loop`/`InferenceAdapter` at all. Building that bridge is a genuine architecture change affecting every adapter, which this remediation explicitly prohibits, so I did not attempt it. What I did fix within scope:
- Added `artifact_verification_state_for`, the previously-missing mapping from the LLM crate's `ArtifactVerificationOutcome` to the storage crate's `LocalArtifactVerificationState` (with its own unit test) — this was genuinely absent, not just unwired.
- Rewrote the daemon's full-pipeline integration test to derive pool capacity and resource requests from an actual `LocalWorkerConfig`/`LocalResourceProfileConfig` (via `define_pools_from_resource_profile`/`execution_resource_requests_for_profile`) instead of hand-picked constants, build the adapter via `LocalInferenceAdapter::from_registry_config`, and exercise `verify_artifact` end-to-end — directly fixing "pool capacities in every test are hand-defined rather than derived from a worker's declared profile."
- This is honestly still short of "a production call site" — that requires the cross-subsystem bridge noted above, which applies equally to every other adapter and belongs to a separate, larger change.

All configured checks pass: `format`, `lint`, and `tests-green-crates` all green in Docker; `familiar-ai-llm`/`familiar-ai-daemon` green apart from the one documented pre-existing flake. No commits made, no scope broadened beyond the 5 already-touched files under `crates/`.
