{"review_id":"00001788454764715789-0001485283-000003-cycle-review-2","reviewed_manifest_hash":"sha256:9bd992ebf6ac96bc93aab5a9dcaf5a6e0eb1046b64119ca95408965a1740ac16","findings":[{"finding_id":"N1-conservative-bootstrap-hits-exhausted-pools","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"SerializeConservatively bootstraps pools that are refused for exhaustion, not for being unknown","claim":"`acquire_with_unknown_capacity_policy` cannot distinguish \"this pool was never defined\" from \"this pool is defined but currently exhausted\": both return `AcquireOutcome::Refused { unavailable }`, and the policy branch then calls `repo.define_pool(&request.pool_id, &request.resource_type, 1, false)` for every entry in `unavailable`. Under contention against an already-defined pool this issues an unintended capacity write against operator-configured capacity — if `define_pool` upserts, a pool defined by `define_pools_from_resource_profile` at `concurrent_inference_slots = 4` is rewritten to capacity 1 while four reservations are still outstanding, so Familiar's own record of observed capacity is smaller than what it has already granted; if `define_pool` ignores existing rows, the write is a silent no-op that contradicts the function's documented contract (\"applying `policy` to any pool Familiar has never observed\"). The existing test only exercises a pool whose capacity is already 1, so neither branch is distinguished by any test.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs","range":{"start":110,"end":135}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs","range":{"start":151,"end":183}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:f0e6e537b4bbb64f6e9305a6a701ca3e9587e8194aeef9818f40f0c1b04d4bda","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":39515,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-63","revision":"sha256:f2b9f39fca0c1d85c39fc877ec01bdbabf72306ff7e175bde43ba6c4d6782016","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-f0e6e537b4bbb64f6e9305a6a701ca3e9587e8194aeef9818f40f0c1b04d4bda-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Determine pool existence explicitly (a `pool_exists`/`describe_pool` query, or a distinct refusal reason carried by `AcquireOutcome::Refused`) and bootstrap the single-occupant pool only for resources with no pool row at all; never call `define_pool` on a pool that already exists. Add a test where a profile-defined pool of capacity > 1 is exhausted and the SerializeConservatively retry is refused without altering the pool's configured capacity.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"N3-telemetry-aggregates-attempts-under-first-id","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"One telemetry row per run, keyed to the first attempt, aggregating every attempt's usage","claim":"`persist_local_telemetry` folds `outcome.attempts` into a single `UsageCategories` and writes one `local_worker_telemetry` row whose `attempt_id` is `outcome.attempts.first()` (or the fabricated sentinel `\"no-attempt\"` when there are none). A multi-turn run therefore records attempts 2..n's token counts under attempt 1's identifier, and per-attempt history is unrecoverable from the ledger even though the schema permits multiple rows per `(execution_id, attempt_id)`. This contradicts the change's own contract text, which states \"Every attempt's typed, timestamped observation is recorded to migration 057's `local_worker_telemetry` table\". The derived `tokens_per_second` compounds the misattribution: it divides the summed output tokens of every turn by one caller-supplied `wall_time_ms` that also spans tool execution between turns, so the stored rate is not a generation rate for any attempt.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs","range":{"start":347,"end":425}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-storage/migrations/057_local_worker_telemetry.sql","range":{"start":9,"end":40}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:d14ca0209daad879bc339c8b6e9de253519dba64378ffb3be35f9deb8c943397","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":112077,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-63","revision":"sha256:f2b9f39fca0c1d85c39fc877ec01bdbabf72306ff7e175bde43ba6c4d6782016","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-d14ca0209daad879bc339c8b6e9de253519dba64378ffb3be35f9deb8c943397-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Record one row per `AttemptUsage` with that attempt's own id, usage and per-attempt measurements, or narrow the contract text and the column to say the row is a run-level aggregate (renaming `attempt_id`, dropping the `\"no-attempt\"` sentinel, and computing `tokens_per_second` only from a per-attempt generation window).","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"N4-hold-on-nothing-executed-failures","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Reservations are held for provider failures the adapter has classified as nothing-executed","claim":"`resolution_for_stop_reason` maps every `StopReason::ProviderFailure { .. }` to `ReservationResolution::HoldUnknown`, discarding the `taxonomy` the loop carries. For `ProviderFailureTaxonomy::Retryable` — the connection-refused/endpoint-never-started case this change's own transport classification and contract describe as \"nothing was executed\" — and for non-retryable failures such as HTTP 401/404, consumption is not unknown but known-zero, yet the reservation is settled with `SettlementObservation::Unknown { policy: HoldReservation }`. With `concurrent_inference_slots = 1` (the profile used in this change's own tests), a developer whose local server is not running or whose credential is wrong has the single inference slot held after each attempt and must wait for PRD-064 owner-liveness recovery before any local execution can be scheduled again.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs","range":{"start":253,"end":313}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/local_runtime.rs","range":{"start":750,"end":772}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:d14ca0209daad879bc339c8b6e9de253519dba64378ffb3be35f9deb8c943397","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":112077,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-63","revision":"sha256:f2b9f39fca0c1d85c39fc877ec01bdbabf72306ff7e175bde43ba6c4d6782016","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-d14ca0209daad879bc339c8b6e9de253519dba64378ffb3be35f9deb8c943397-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Match on the taxonomy: release (or commit zero observed consumption) for failures the adapter classifies as nothing-executed, and hold only for `Ambiguous`/`Timeout`, where the endpoint may have begun executing. Add a test asserting that a refused connection releases the slot so a subsequent execution can acquire it.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"N5-policy-registration-silently-ignores-divergence","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Allocation policy re-registration silently keeps a divergent stored policy, and estimates are never cross-checked against it","claim":"`register_allocation_policy` uses `INSERT OR IGNORE` against the `(policy_id, policy_version)` primary key, so re-registering the same identity with different `kind`, `currency`, `declared_assumptions_json`, or `enabled` value returns `Ok(())` while silently retaining the previously stored row — the doc comment's \"registers (or replays, if identical)\" is not enforced, since identity is never compared to content. `record_allocation_estimate` then stores the caller's own `currency` and `declared_assumptions_json` on the estimate row without comparing them to the referenced policy's, so an audit row can name a policy identity and version whose stored assumptions and currency contradict the figures recorded under it, in a table whose stated purpose is auditable provenance for operator-allocated money amounts.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-storage/src/repos/local_telemetry.rs","range":{"start":240,"end":340}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-storage/migrations/057_local_worker_telemetry.sql","range":{"start":45,"end":75}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:f0e6e537b4bbb64f6e9305a6a701ca3e9587e8194aeef9818f40f0c1b04d4bda","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":39515,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-63","revision":"sha256:f2b9f39fca0c1d85c39fc877ec01bdbabf72306ff7e175bde43ba6c4d6782016","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-f0e6e537b4bbb64f6e9305a6a701ca3e9587e8194aeef9818f40f0c1b04d4bda-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Read back the stored row on registration and return `FamiliarError::Config` when an existing `(policy_id, policy_version)` differs in any field, instead of `INSERT OR IGNORE`; reject an estimate whose `currency` or `declared_assumptions_json` disagrees with its policy row. Add storage tests for conflicting re-registration and for a currency-mismatched estimate.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"N2-toolcall-complete-order-nondeterministic","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"ToolCallComplete events for parallel tool calls are emitted in HashMap iteration order","claim":"`consume_stream` accumulates streamed tool calls in a `HashMap<u64, PendingCall>` and, after the terminal frame, emits `StreamEvent::ToolCallComplete` by iterating that map (`for (index, call) in &pending`). Rust's default `HashMap` hasher is randomly seeded per process, so when one assistant turn returns two or more tool calls the completion order — and therefore the order in which the loop validates, authorizes, journals, and executes those calls — varies between otherwise identical runs against identical responses, in a subsystem whose journal and `ResumePoint { journal_high_water_mark }` depend on a stable call order for replay and resumption. No test in the change exercises more than one tool call per turn, so the passing suite cannot surface this.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/local_runtime.rs","range":{"start":517,"end":665}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:f0e6e537b4bbb64f6e9305a6a701ca3e9587e8194aeef9818f40f0c1b04d4bda","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":39515,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-63","revision":"sha256:f2b9f39fca0c1d85c39fc877ec01bdbabf72306ff7e175bde43ba6c4d6782016","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-f0e6e537b4bbb64f6e9305a6a701ca3e9587e8194aeef9818f40f0c1b04d4bda-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Use a `BTreeMap<u64, PendingCall>` (or sort by the backend's `index` before emitting completions) so completion order always follows the wire order, and add a fake-runtime test with two tool calls in one turn asserting a fixed execution order.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"N7-buffered-body-defeats-streaming-and-ttft","category":"maintainability_issue","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"The transport buffers the whole response, so streaming, TTFT, and cancellation are structurally unavailable while the schema invites a TTFT value anyway","claim":"`LocalChatClient::submit` calls `response.text().await` and only then replays SSE frames to the observer, so no event reaches the loop before the complete response has arrived: mid-response cancellation has nothing to interrupt (acknowledged by the adapter's no-op `cancel` comment) and time to first token cannot be observed at this boundary at all. Migration 057 nevertheless carries a `time_to_first_token_ms` column and `LocalRunMeasurements` a `time_to_first_token_ms` field, and any caller that fills them from around `submit` is recording full-response latency labelled as time to first token — a fabricated measurement in a ledger whose stated discipline is that unmeasured fields stay absent.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/local_runtime.rs","range":{"start":330,"end":380}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs","range":{"start":329,"end":345}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:f0e6e537b4bbb64f6e9305a6a701ca3e9587e8194aeef9818f40f0c1b04d4bda","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":39515,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-63","revision":"sha256:f2b9f39fca0c1d85c39fc877ec01bdbabf72306ff7e175bde43ba6c4d6782016","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-f0e6e537b4bbb64f6e9305a6a701ca3e9587e8194aeef9818f40f0c1b04d4bda-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Either consume the response with `bytes_stream()` and emit events (and a first-token timestamp) as frames arrive, honouring the cancellation token between frames, or state in the contract that TTFT is unavailable in phase 1 and have the transport itself supply the only permitted `time_to_first_token_ms` value so no caller can populate it with whole-response latency.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"N6-local-worker-unreachable-from-production","category":"unverifiable_claim","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"No production path constructs a local worker: every new entry point is reached only from tests","claim":"Within the disclosed diff, `LocalInferenceAdapter::new`/`from_registry_config`, `verify_artifact`, `probe_health`, `execution_resource_requests(_for_profile)`, `define_pools_from_resource_profile`, `acquire_with_unknown_capacity_policy`, `acquire_model_load_reservation`, `thermal_or_power_ceiling_exceeded`, `resolve_reservation` and `persist_local_telemetry` are called only from `#[cfg(test)]` modules and integration tests; nothing dispatches a validated `provider = \"local\"` registry entry to the new adapter, and the only non-test edits outside the new files are `pub mod` declarations and `local: None` struct-literal fields. A `[worker_registry.workers.<id>.local]` entry therefore validates but can never be routed, executed, reserved against, or recorded, so I cannot verify the acceptance criteria that a local worker is a routable PRD-057 worker whose execution consumes PRD-064 reservations and lands in the PRD-051-adjacent ledger. The `lint` gate cannot surface this because it runs with `-A dead-code`.","evidence":[{"kind":"verification","check_id":"lint","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:35da19fdddf55ea414c62dbbe1da5c0312148d1021236904700b9a150357b8ee","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":1268,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-63","revision":"sha256:f2b9f39fca0c1d85c39fc877ec01bdbabf72306ff7e175bde43ba6c4d6782016","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-35da19fdddf55ea414c62dbbe1da5c0312148d1021236904700b9a150357b8ee-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/local_worker.rs","range":{"start":24,"end":110}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs","range":{"start":1,"end":30}},{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/lib.rs","hunk":"@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ pub mod delivery;\n pub mod drive;\n pub mod launchd;\n pub mod local_transport;\n+pub mod local_worker_runtime;\n pub mod openai_billing;\n pub mod plan;\n pub mod preflight;"}],"remediation":"Wire the local path into the daemon's real execution route — dispatch a `provider = \"local\"` worker with a `local` profile to `LocalInferenceAdapter`, acquire/resolve its reservations and persist its telemetry from that route — and cover it with a test that starts from a registry config rather than from hand-constructed adapters and pools. If wiring is deliberately deferred, say so in the contract's scope section and in the task's acceptance record rather than leaving the criteria implicitly claimed.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F6-new-crates-not-covered-by-passing-check","category":"unverifiable_claim","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"New llm and daemon code is still covered only by the failing advisory workspace check","claim":"Unchanged this cycle: the required `tests-green-crates` check still runs only `familiar-ai-core`, `familiar-ai-review`, `familiar-ai-agent` and `familiar-ai-storage`, so `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/local_runtime.rs` (1103 lines), `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs` (911 lines) and `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/local_worker_runtime.rs` (408 lines) are exercised only by `tests-workspace-advisory`, which exited 101 (status failed, required false). I therefore still cannot confirm that the new llm/daemon tests pass or that this change does not break existing workspace tests.","evidence":[{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:d14ca0209daad879bc339c8b6e9de253519dba64378ffb3be35f9deb8c943397","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":112077,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-63","revision":"sha256:f2b9f39fca0c1d85c39fc877ec01bdbabf72306ff7e175bde43ba6c4d6782016","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-d14ca0209daad879bc339c8b6e9de253519dba64378ffb3be35f9deb8c943397-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:f0e6e537b4bbb64f6e9305a6a701ca3e9587e8194aeef9818f40f0c1b04d4bda","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":39515,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-63","revision":"sha256:f2b9f39fca0c1d85c39fc877ec01bdbabf72306ff7e175bde43ba6c4d6782016","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-f0e6e537b4bbb64f6e9305a6a701ca3e9587e8194aeef9818f40f0c1b04d4bda-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Add `-p familiar-ai-llm -p familiar-ai-daemon` to the required `tests-green-crates` check (or make the workspace check required) and resolve whatever makes `tests-workspace-advisory` exit 101, so the crates carrying the bulk of this change are gated by a passing check.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F1-retries-counts-iterations","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"retries no longer derived from attempt count","claim":"Resolved. `persist_local_telemetry` now takes `retries: u32` from the caller instead of deriving `outcome.attempts.len().saturating_sub(1)`, its doc comment states why `attempts.len()` counts loop turns rather than retries, and `multi_attempt_successful_run_records_zero_retries_not_attempt_count` asserts that a three-submission successful run stores `retries = 0`. The remaining honesty risk in this function is separate and reported as N3-telemetry-aggregates-attempts-under-first-id.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs","range":{"start":347,"end":425}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:d14ca0209daad879bc339c8b6e9de253519dba64378ffb3be35f9deb8c943397","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":112077,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-63","revision":"sha256:f2b9f39fca0c1d85c39fc877ec01bdbabf72306ff7e175bde43ba6c4d6782016","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-d14ca0209daad879bc339c8b6e9de253519dba64378ffb3be35f9deb8c943397-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"No further action for this finding; keep the caller-supplied `retries` contract documented when resumption tracking is added.","status":"resolved","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F4-tls-field-unenforced","category":"security_issue","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"Credential over plaintext non-loopback endpoints now refused at both layers","claim":"Resolved. Registry validation now refuses a non-loopback `local` endpoint unless `auth_profile` is set and both `tls = true` and an `https://` `base_url` are present, and also refuses a declared `tls = true` that disagrees with the URL scheme; independently, `LocalChatClient::new` fails closed via `credential_safe_transport` when a bearer credential would be attached to a plaintext non-loopback endpoint, so the previously ignored `tls` flag is now load-bearing and the cleartext-credential path in `authorize` is unreachable. Unit tests cover the plaintext-LAN refusal, the https-LAN acceptance, the plaintext-loopback acceptance, and the no-credential case.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/registry_workers.rs","range":{"start":695,"end":744}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/local_runtime.rs","range":{"start":56,"end":140}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/registry_workers.rs","range":{"start":246,"end":394}}],"remediation":"No further action for this finding.","status":"resolved","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F7-local-profile-not-wired","category":"unverifiable_claim","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"Superseded by a narrower statement of the remaining wiring gap","claim":"Partly addressed, partly still present, so restated. The half of this finding about unread profile fields is now invalid: `define_pools_from_resource_profile` reads `concurrent_inference_slots` and `model_loading_slots` as pool capacities, `execution_resource_requests_for_profile` derives the per-execution requests from the profile, `thermal_or_power_ceiling_exceeded` reads the thermal and power ceilings, and `LocalInferenceAdapter::from_registry_config` builds the adapter from a `LocalWorkerConfig`. The half about there being no production caller is unchanged and is restated precisely as N6-local-worker-unreachable-from-production.","evidence":[{"kind":"verification","check_id":"lint","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:35da19fdddf55ea414c62dbbe1da5c0312148d1021236904700b9a150357b8ee","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":1268,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-63","revision":"sha256:f2b9f39fca0c1d85c39fc877ec01bdbabf72306ff7e175bde43ba6c4d6782016","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-35da19fdddf55ea414c62dbbe1da5c0312148d1021236904700b9a150357b8ee-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs","range":{"start":135,"end":210}}],"remediation":"Track the remaining work under N6-local-worker-unreachable-from-production.","status":"superseded","supersedes":"N6-local-worker-unreachable-from-production"}]}
